{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Las Vegas Monorail is a 3.9 mi monorail mass transit system located adjacent to the Las Vegas Strip, in Clark County, Nevada, United States.","title":"Las Vegas Monorail"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It connects several large casinos in the unincorporated communities of Paradise and Winchester, and does not enter the City of Las Vegas.","title":"Las Vegas Monorail"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is owned and operated by the Las Vegas Monorail Company.","title":"Las Vegas Monorail"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In 2013, total annual ridership was roughly 4.2 million, down from a pre-Great Recession peak of 7.9 million in 2007.","title":"Las Vegas Monorail"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The monorail is a registered not-for-profit corporation, allowed under Nevada law since the monorail provides a public service.","title":"Las Vegas Monorail"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The State of Nevada assisted in bond financing, but no public money was used in construction.","title":"Las Vegas Monorail"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Initiative for Interstellar Studies (i4is) was founded in London in 2012 as a not-for-profit unincorporated organisation.","title":"Initiative for Interstellar Studies"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Its stated objectives are education and research into the challenges of Interstellar Travel.","title":"Initiative for Interstellar Studies"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" i4is was incorporated in the UK in May 2014 as a not-for-profit company limited by guarantee (Companies House number:09062458).","title":"Initiative for Interstellar Studies"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Its original title of Institute for Interstellar Studies reflects the stated ambitions of the company.","title":"Initiative for Interstellar Studies"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Guidance Residential LLC.","title":"Guidance Residential"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" is a U.S. based Islamic home financing company headquartered in Reston, Virginia.","title":"Guidance Residential"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Guidance Residential is the largest Islamic home financing provider in the United States by total market share in the niche market.","title":"Guidance Residential"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The company started operation in 2002 to provide Shariah compliant, riba-free (free of interest or usury) home financing contracts to Muslim American home buyers.","title":"Guidance Residential"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Guidance Residential is a wholly owned subsidiary of Guidance Financial Group, which is a subsidiary of the parent company, Capital Guidance.","title":"Guidance Residential"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The company has funded over $4.5 billion in Islamic home financing in American Muslim real estate market through its Declining Balance Co-Ownership Program.","title":"Guidance Residential"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The Declining Balance Co-Ownership Program is a Shariah-compliant structure of home financing based on "Diminishing Musharakah" or Equity Partnership model which is a non-lending method of home financing and is unique to the Islamic home financing market in the United States.","title":"Guidance Residential"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Mark IV monorail was a design model of straddle-type monorail trains.","title":"Mark IV monorail"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The design was developed by legendary Disney Imagineer Bob Gurr.","title":"Mark IV monorail"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Ten trains were built by Martin Marietta in 1969 at the cost of about $7 million USD each and they were used on the Walt Disney World Monorail System between 1971 and 1989 before they were replaced by the Mark VI monorail, although a few lasted until 1991.","title":"Mark IV monorail"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Sometime between 1991 and 1994 Monorail Coral and Lime (which had been introduced new in 1984) were sold for $3.5 million each, refurbished, and used to begin the Las Vegas Monorail operations.","title":"Mark IV monorail"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In 2004 Lime and Coral (now the MGM and Bally) were replaced by fully automated Bombardier MVI 4-car trains.","title":"Mark IV monorail"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Kiwi Advanced Research and Education Network (KAREN), now known simply as the REANNZ Network, is a high-capacity, ultra high-speed national research and education network (NREN) connecting New Zealand's tertiary institutions, research organisations, libraries, schools and museums, and the rest of the world.","title":"Kiwi Advanced Research and Education Network"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" REANNZ (Research and Education Advanced Network New Zealand Ltd), a Crown-owned not-for-profit company, owns and operates KAREN.","title":"Kiwi Advanced Research and Education Network"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Mark VI monorail (or M-VI) is a monorail train used in the Walt Disney World Monorail System and the Las Vegas Monorail.","title":"Mark VI monorail"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The Mark VI started replacing the Mark IV monorails at Walt Disney World in 1989, replacing the final Mark IV by 1991.","title":"Mark VI monorail"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Las Vegas M-VI versions of the trains differ from the Walt Disney World trains in both physical appearance and in that the trains are automated.","title":"Mark VI monorail"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: State of Nevada
