{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Sub is an American short horror film directed by Dan Samiljan, co-written by Dave Cain and Samiljan, and produced by Justin Wagman and Noelle Hubbell.","title":"The Sub"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film stars Zoe Jarman, Heather Langenkamp and Brian Stepanek.","title":"The Sub"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The film had a successful Kickstarter campaign.","title":"The Sub"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Heather Elizabeth Langenkamp (born July 17, 1964) is an American actress, make-up artist and producer.","title":"Heather Langenkamp"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She is best known for her role as Nancy Thompson in "A Nightmare on Elm Street" (1984) and the sequel "" (1987), as well as in cult films such as two of Wes Craven's films: "Shocker" (1989) and "Wes Craven's New Nightmare" (1994).","title":"Heather Langenkamp"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She served as executive producer and narrator to the 2010 documentary "".","title":"Heather Langenkamp"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Her other film roles include "Nickel Mountain" (1984), "The Demolitionist" (1995), "The Butterfly Room" (2012), "Star Trek Into Darkness" (2013), and "Truth or Dare" (2017).","title":"Heather Langenkamp"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Langenkamp is also known for her roles as Marie Lubbock and Amy Boutilier on the sitcom "Growing Pains" (1988-1990) and the spin-off series "Just the Ten of Us" (1988–1990), and has had numerous television guest appearances.","title":"Heather Langenkamp"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Simon Mark Monjack (9 March 1970 – 23 May 2010) was a British screenwriter, film director, film producer and make-up artist.","title":"Simon Monjack"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was the husband of American actress Brittany Murphy.","title":"Simon Monjack"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Charis Elisa Michelsen (born December 30, 1974) is an American actress, a former model and a make-up artist.","title":"Charis Michelsen"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Michelsen worked as a model in New York City in her early adulthood before beginning a career as an actress.","title":"Charis Michelsen"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She appeared in supporting roles in the films "High Art" (1998), Martin Scorsese's "Bringing Out the Dead" (1999), and "Wonder Boys" (2000).","title":"Charis Michelsen"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Montague George "Monty" Westmore (June 12, 1923 – November 13, 2007) was part of the third generation of the Westmore family of American make-up artists in film and television who worked on over 75 films and television series since 1950.","title":"Monty Westmore"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was the brother of make-up artist Michael Westmore and uncle of actress McKenzie Westmore.","title":"Monty Westmore"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Cameron Clayton (born September 11, 1993), better known by his stage name Farrah Moan, is an American drag queen, model, make-up artist and internet personality.","title":"Farrah Moan"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is best known for his participation in the ninth season of Emmy Award-winning reality TV show "RuPaul's Drag Race", where he placed eighth.","title":"Farrah Moan"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" His stage name is a pun on the chemical "pheromone", whilst also being a reference to American actress Farrah Fawcett.","title":"Farrah Moan"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In some interviews, Clayton jokingly states that his drag surname is a reference to "being a whore".","title":"Farrah Moan"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Heather Langenkamp
